    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (71.83) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.52) anchoring the offense as our clear top-tier starters. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite facing Leiter, as his elite .421 xwOBA provides an immense ceiling that neutralizes park factors. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a quintessential \"Zebras special\" today; while he occupies the #8 spot, the matchup against Burke provides an extraordinary 14% boost via platoon advantage, and the opposing pitcher's slow delivery creates a high-probability environment for him to exploit our league's scarcity in stolen bases. **Junior Caminero** (65.41) also offers strong output, as a favorable matchup against Junk allows him to capitalize on his #2 order positioning.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the benching of **Carson Benge** (49.21), who fell just shy of the active rotation despite a strong profile. While **Carson Benge** benefits from a lead-off spot, the optimizer favored the higher reliability of **Luke Raley** (60.21) against V\u00e1squez. **Luke Raley** is positioned to outperform his base projection due to a significant 19% SP skill boost, making him a more efficient use of our game caps than the higher-risk floor offered by **Carson Benge**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Casey Schmitt** (63.92); though his spot is pending official confirmation, our assumption of him batting #3 against Civale is driving his high score.\n\nWe must remain cautious with **Trea Turner** (54.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.13), as both face Ashcraft, whose 3.52 xERA acts as a significant drag on their offensive potential. While **Trea Turner** retains value through his #1 slotting, the SP skill penalty is non-trivial. Similarly, **Dillon Dingler** (43.91) is on the borderline of our efficiency threshold; he remains active, but should we see any late-hour lineup shifts, he is the first candidate to be pulled to preserve caps if a higher-upside pivot like **Chase Meidroth** becomes viable.",
